    {
      "section_id": "trainingmobileappdevelopment_06_detail_section",
      "section_order": 6,
      "html_id": null,
      "element": "section",
      "section_name": "Detail Section",
      "section_heading": "Good questions.",
      "heading_level": "h2",
      "eyebrow": "A little more clarity",
      "subheading": "",
      "description": "",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A little more clarity",
        "Yes, where practical, and under NDA if required. Working inside (or on a sanitized copy of) your actual app is the fastest way to reduce the single-person dependency most teams come to us with.",
        "Natively, no; this track is Android-first. Flutter, which the program covers in depth, ships to both Android and iOS from one codebase, and for most teams that's the practical route to iOS.",
        "Manageable, and common: web developers are half our attendees. Flutter's widget model feels familiar to React developers, and the program is paced for exactly this transition."
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "A little more clarity"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Good questions."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Can the training focus on our existing app's codebase?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Yes, where practical, and under NDA if required. Working inside (or on a sanitized copy of) your actual app is the fastest way to reduce the single-person dependency most teams come to us with."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Do you cover iOS?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Natively, no; this track is Android-first. Flutter, which the program covers in depth, ships to both Android and iOS from one codebase, and for most teams that's the practical route to iOS."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Our developers only know web (React/JS). How steep is the jump?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Manageable, and common: web developers are half our attendees. Flutter's widget model feels familiar to React developers, and the program is paced for exactly this transition."
        }
      ],
